{
  "title": "Realtime Speech Interpreter: architecture",
  "desc": "Audio leaves the venue mixer, goes through OBS and SRT to a Network Load Balancer and a Fargate app. The app calls Transcribe, Translate or Bedrock, and Polly, then publishes Japanese audio to a LiveKit server on EC2. Listener browsers play the audio. A CloudFront, S3 and Lambda path serves the page and subscribe-only tokens. Secrets Manager and CloudWatch Logs support the pipeline.",
